  "sentences": [
   "The Sydney Opera House stands as one of the most recognisable buildings in the world today.",
   "Located on the edge of Sydney Harbour in New South Wales, Australia, it serves as a leading centre for the performing arts.",
   "Its distinctive shell-shaped roof has become a powerful symbol of both the city and the nation.",
   "Millions of visitors travel to the site each year to admire its remarkable design.",
   "The building was designed by the Danish architect J\u00f8rn Utzon, who won an international competition in 1957.",
   "Construction began in 1959 and continued for more than a decade, facing significant delays and rising costs along the way.",
   "Utzon eventually resigned from the project before it was completed.",
   "The building was formally opened by Queen Elizabeth II in 1973, marking a major milestone in Australian cultural history.",
   "The Opera House is home to a wide range of performance spaces, including the Concert Hall, the Joan Sutherland Theatre, and the Drama Theatre.",
   "These venues host thousands of performances every year, covering opera, classical music, theatre, and contemporary entertainment.",
   "The site is used by several resident companies, which contribute to a rich and varied artistic programme.",
   "As a result, the building plays a vital role in the cultural life of Australia.",
   "The architecture of the Opera House is widely regarded as a masterpiece of modern design.",
   "The interlocking shells that form the roof were an ambitious engineering challenge for their time.",
   "Innovative solutions were required to bring the original vision to life, and these methods influenced construction techniques around the world.",
   "The building continues to be studied by architects and engineers today.",
   "In 2007, the Sydney Opera House was added to the UNESCO World Heritage List in recognition of its outstanding value.",
   "It remains a testament to creative ambition and technical achievement.",
   "The site attracts visitors from every corner of the globe, and it continues to serve as an active venue for the arts.",
   "Today, the Sydney Opera House represents a lasting symbol of Australian identity and cultural pride."
  ]
